  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular solutions to plastic pollution in South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to reduce volumes of plastic waste generated and leaked into the environment through the implementation of strategic circular interventions upstream and midstream in the plastic packaging value chain in the food and beverage sector in South Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the national priorities of creating economic opportunities especially for the vulnerable, a just transition lens is needed for all proposed outputs and activities. Through the planned upstream and midstream interventions, job creation is forecast to increase across all genders and skill levels relative to the baseline based on previous research in South Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
